  "description": "The Computer Retrieval of Information on Scientific Projects (CRISP) Thesaurus was developed by the National Institutes of Health for use in the CRISP database of research projects funded by the U.S. Public Health Service (PHS).\r\n\r\nCRISP contains over 8,000 preferred terms that are grouped hierarchically into 11 domains. The 11 domains are:\r\n\r\n- anatomy\r\n- behavioral/social science\r\n- biology\r\n- chemical\r\n- disease/disorder\r\n- food science/technology\r\n- medicine\r\n- named group\r\n- organism\r\n- physical science\r\ntechnology/technique",
